 "calibre_note": "with equal terminal flows and binary bifurcations, Murray ties the trunk and terminal radii together through n_downstream^(1/3). Spanning the real 20-40x radius ratio of a named trunk down to a 0.3 mm adventitial branch would need n = 8000-64000 terminals. With 34-97 terminals per tree the span is only 3.2-4.6x, so the terminal calibres were anchored to the published small-vessel range and FOUR of the seven trunk calibres consequently fall BELOW their published diameters (inferior thyroid artery -16%, inferior thyroid vein -28%, left gastric vein -54%, azygos -58%). No radius was adjusted to hide this."
